To Whom It May Concern:

Pursuant to the Connecticut Freedom of Information Act, I hereby request the following records:

1. A complete copy of the Stamford Police Department Policy and Procedure Manual (including all General Orders, Standard Operating Procedures, Directives, and any other written rules, policies, or procedures governing the conduct of Department personnel) as it existed and was in effect during calendar year 2019, together with any table of contents, index, or list of policy numbers and titles for that manual. If any policy was revised during 2019, please produce each version in effect at any point during that year, with its effective date.

2. Without limiting Item 1, the following policies, procedures, General Orders, or directives as in effect during calendar year 2019:

(a) Collection, handling, documentation, packaging, and preservation of physical evidence, including crime scene processing and chain of custody;
(b) Seizure of evidence and property, both pursuant to a warrant and without a warrant, including consent searches, searches incident to arrest, plain view, exigent circumstances, and inventory searches;
(c) Motor vehicle stops, motor vehicle searches, and the towing, impoundment, and inventory of motor vehicles;
(d) Interviews of witnesses, including the recording and documentation of witness statements;
(e) Interviews and interrogations of suspects and arrestees, including Miranda advisement and waiver, and the electronic recording of custodial interrogations;
(f) Body-worn cameras and dashboard/in-car cameras, including activation, deactivation, review, and retention of recordings;
(g) Audio and video recording in interview and interrogation rooms, including retention of those recordings;
(h) Lock-up, holding cell, booking, and prisoner processing and detention procedures;
(i) Audio and video recording of lock-up, holding cell, booking, and prisoner processing areas;
(j) Retention, storage, preservation, and destruction of video and audio recordings of every kind generated or maintained by the Department, including any records retention schedule the Department followed in 2019.

3. Any index, log, or memorandum identifying the policies issued, revised, or rescinded during calendar year 2019, sufficient to establish which version of each policy was in effect on any given date that year.

I am an attorney admitted to practice in Connecticut, serving as assigned counsel on behalf of the State of Connecticut Office of the Chief Public Defender, and these records are sought in connection with the representation of an indigent criminal defendant.

Pursuant to Conn. Gen. Stat. § 1-212(d)(5), I request that all fees be waived. I am an attorney appointed by the court as Division of Public Defender Services assigned counsel under Conn. Gen. Stat. § 51-296, and I hereby certify that the records requested pertain to my duties in that capacity.

To the extent the Department contends that any portion of any policy is exempt from disclosure under Conn. Gen. Stat. § 1-210(b), I request that the Department disclose all non-exempt portions, identify each withheld policy by number and title, and state the specific statutory exemption claimed for each withholding, as required by the Freedom of Information Act.

Please produce the records in electronic (PDF) format. Several of the Department's policies are already published in that form on the City's website, and I request that the remaining policies be produced in the same manner.

I also request that, if possible and pursuant to Conn. Gen. Stat. § 1-212(d), fees be waived as I believe this request is in the public interest and not made for commercial gain. The requested documents will be made available to the public at MuckRock.com.

In the event that there are fees, I would be grateful if you would inform me of the total charges in advance of fulfilling my request. I would prefer the request filled electronically, by e-mail attachment if available or CD-ROM if not.

Thank you in advance for your anticipated cooperation in this matter. I look forward to receiving your response to this request within 4 business days, as the statute requires.

Sincerely,

Dean E Popkin
